---
import Walkthrough from "./Walkthrough.astro";
---

<Walkthrough kind="disclosure">
  <div class="article">
    <div class="article-label">Field notes · 01</div>
    <h2>A quieter interface</h2>
    <p>
      A useful interface makes
      <button
        disabled
        class="term"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="detail-one"
      >
        the next action legible</button
      ><span id="detail-one" class="expansion" hidden
        ><span class="note-number">01 / intent</span>The label should say what
        happens when you use it. “save draft” tells you more than “continue.”
        <button
          disabled
          class="term"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="detail-nested"
        >
          Why does that matter?</button
        ><span id="detail-nested" class="expansion nested" hidden
          >The user can predict the result without first taking the risk.
          Clarity is useful even when an action is reversible.</span
        ></span
      >
      without explaining every possible action at once.
    </p>
    <p>
      One way to do that is
      <button
        disabled
        class="term"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="detail-two"
      >
        progressive disclosure</button
      ><span id="detail-two" class="expansion" hidden
        ><span class="note-number">02 / depth</span>Start with the short
        version. Let someone request more detail where they need it, while
        keeping the surrounding argument available.</span
      >. The tradeoff is that each expansion moves the text below it.
    </p>
    <p class="closing">
      The question: does staying on the page also mean keeping your place?
    </p>
  </div>
</Walkthrough>
<style>
  .article {
    margin-top: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--edge);
    background: var(--paper);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 28px;
  }
  .article-label {
    font:
      12px ui-monospace,
      monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--secondary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .article h2 {
    margin: 0.83em 0;
    font:
      normal 29px/1.2 Georgia,
      serif;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  .article p {
    margin: 12px 0;
    font:
      19px/1.8 Georgia,
      serif;
  }
  .term {
    display: inline-block;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding-inline: 3px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);
    background: var(--highlight);
    color: var(--green);
    font: inherit;
    line-height: inherit;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .term[aria-expanded="true"] {
    background: var(--highlight);
    border-bottom-style: solid;
  }
  .expansion {
    display: block;
    font:
      15px/1.7 system-ui,
      sans-serif;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--edge);
    margin: 16px 0;
    padding: 3px 0 3px 18px;
    color: var(--secondary);
  }
  .expansion[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .nested {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .note-number {
    display: block;
    font:
      12px ui-monospace,
      monospace;
    color: var(--secondary);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .article p.closing {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--secondary);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--edge);
    padding-top: 18px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 440px) {
    .article {
      padding: 20px;
    }
    .article p {
      font-size: 18px;
    }
  }
</style>
